[i][DEMO GIF SLOT — CQC melee draw / warmup swap clip goes here at publish][/i]

Makes [b]Combat Extended[/b] and [b]Simple Sidearms[/b] actually work together. Both mods ship zero knowledge of each other; this patch repairs every seam found by cross-reading both codebases — repair only, no new behavior, both mods work as their authors intended.

[h1]What it fixes[/h1]
[list]
[*]Sidearm carry limits now respect CE's inventory system (weight [i]and[/i] bulk) - including the weapons Simple Sidearms goes and fetches by itself.
[*]Weapon ranking uses real CE damage numbers, so pawns actually pick the better gun.
[*]Pawns never auto-switch to a gun that has no ammo.
[*]Enemies spawn with their sidearms loaded and carrying spare ammo.
[*]Switching weapons no longer interrupts a reload partway through.
[*]Drawing a melee sidearm when attacked in melee works again.
[*]Mid-fight auto-switching to a better-suited gun works again.
[*]Firing a single-use launcher leaves the pawn holding their preferred backup, not fists.
[*]When a gun runs dry or is destroyed, the replacement follows your sidearm preferences instead of CE's guess.
[*]CE loadout enforcement no longer strips remembered sidearms out of inventories.
[*]EMP and incendiary weapon detection matches the ammo actually loaded.
[/list]

Technical details per fix: see the [url=https://github.com/eebette/CombatExtended-SimpleSidearms-Compatibility-Patch]GitHub README[/url] ("What it fixes (for nerds)").

[h1]Load order[/h1]
Harmony → Combat Extended → Simple Sidearms → this mod (declared in About.xml; the game sorts it for you).

[h1]Good to know[/h1]
[list]
[*]Safe to add or remove mid-save.
[*]SS-remembered weapons are exempt from CE loadout drops by design — SS memory is explicit player intent. Forget the sidearm to let CE drop it.
[*][b]Melee Animation[/b]: animated execution kills bypass the melee-attack hook, so the CQC auto-draw doesn't trigger during those — everything else works.
[*]On a fresh Simple Sidearms install its "Basic" settings preset auto-applies; the patch works with any preset.
[/list]

[h1]My other mods[/h1]
[b]The CE + Simple Sidearms suite[/b] — two optional modules that require this patch. This patch only repairs what the two mods break in each other; anything that would change how they behave lives out here.
[list]
[*][b]Compatibility Module - Loadouts[/b] — CE loadouts and SS memory as one idea: loadout weapons remembered as sidearms, roles by list order, ammo kept stocked. For you if you manage kit through CE loadouts and keep teaching new recruits their sidearms by hand.
[*][b]Compatibility Module - Tactics[/b] — better triggers for WHEN a pawn changes weapon: don't abandon a reload, break DPS ties on carried ammo, draw a melee weapon that can hurt what's in front of you. For you if your pawns pick sensible weapons at senseless moments.
[/list]
[b]Standalone[/b] — neither needs this patch, or each other.
[list]
[*][b]Better Attack Orders for Simple Sidearms[/b] — Simple Sidearms only, no CE. Attack orders consider every gun the pawn carries, instead of only the one in hand.
[*][b]Loadout Quality for Combat Extended[/b] — CE only, no Simple Sidearms. Per-loadout quality and durability floors, plus self-upgrading when a better copy turns up.
[*][b]Universal Patch for More Materials[/b] — no weapons involved. More Materials adds copper, tin and nickel to vanilla recipes only; this derives the rules behind those choices and applies them to every content mod you have, including ones released after it.
[/list]

